From: erenmakal <69559506+erenmakal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Optional cancellable cactus age changes

Paper #13480 documents that BlockGrowEvent covers formation of the new cactus
block but not the root cactus' own AGE state updates. Plugins therefore cannot
stop the age from reaching 15 by cancelling BlockGrowEvent.

When enabled, route the self AGE update through the same Bukkit grow helper.
This intentionally strengthens the event contract and is switchable in
folia.yml for plugins that depend on upstream behaviour.


diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/CactusBlock.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/CactusBlock.java
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/CactusBlock.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/CactusBlock.java
@@ -79,7 +79,13 @@ public class CactusBlock extends Block {
                 level.neighborChanged(aboveBlock, above, this, null, false);
             } else if (age < 15) {
-                level.setBlock(pos, state.setValue(AGE, age + 1), Block.UPDATE_NONE);
+                // Folia performance pack - Paper #13480
+                final BlockState agedState = state.setValue(AGE, age + 1);
+                if (dev.eren.folia.config.FoliaConfig.cancellableCactusAge) {
+                    org.bukkit.craftbukkit.event.CraftEventFactory.handleBlockGrowEvent(level, pos, agedState, Block.UPDATE_NONE);
+                } else {
+                    level.setBlock(pos, agedState, Block.UPDATE_NONE);
+                }
             }
         }
     }
